From: Pavankumar Nandeshwar <pnandesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 4 Aug 2025 19:18:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: batch PPE completion NAPI service

The QSDK PPEDS completion NAPI handles up to 256 completion records per
poll and charges those records to NAPI at a four-to-one ratio.  The native
direct-switch implementation services one completion per NAPI budget unit,
which can leave the WBM PPE completion ring as the throughput limiter under
sustained multi-gigabit downlink traffic.

Keep the native generic IRQ-group and SRNG locking model, but give its PPE
completion path the same bounded batch size.  If the bounded service budget
is exhausted, report the whole NAPI budget so the poll remains scheduled;
otherwise report the amortized work count.  This prevents an incomplete
completion ring from being mistaken for an idle one.

Based-on: 41c027804556a6adc68fa0d79400fb96655a909e
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0486-QSDK-DP-wifi-ath12k-Fixes-to-improve-DS-DL-performan.patch
Signed-off-by: Pavankumar Nandeshwar <pnandesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c  | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
@@ -941,6 +941,10 @@ int ath12k_dp_service_srng(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 	int tot_work_done = 0;
 	enum dp_monitor_mode monitor_mode;
 	u8 ring_mask;
+#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH12K_PPE_DS_SUPPORT
+	int ppeds_budget;
+	int ppeds_done;
+#endif
 
 #ifdef CPTCFG_ATH12K_PPE_DS_SUPPORT
 	if (ab->hw_params->ring_mask->ppe2tcl[grp_id])
@@ -950,7 +954,23 @@ int ath12k_dp_service_srng(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 		ath12k_ppe_ds_service_reo2ppe(ab);
 
 	if (ab->hw_params->ring_mask->ppeds_tx_cmpl[grp_id]) {
-		work_done = ath12k_ppe_ds_service_tx_completion(ab, budget);
+		ppeds_budget = min_t(int,
+			budget * ATH12K_PPE_DS_TX_CMPL_NAPI_SCALE - 1,
+			ATH12K_PPE_DS_TX_CMPL_MAX_BUDGET);
+		ppeds_done = ath12k_ppe_ds_service_tx_completion(ab,
+							ppeds_budget);
+
+		/*
+		 * QSDK amortizes four PPEDS completions into one NAPI work item.
+		 * A full bounded batch may still leave ring entries pending, so
+		 * consume the remaining NAPI budget to keep polling in that case.
+		 */
+		if (ppeds_done == ppeds_budget)
+			work_done = budget;
+		else
+			work_done = DIV_ROUND_UP(ppeds_done,
+						 ATH12K_PPE_DS_TX_CMPL_NAPI_SCALE);
+
 		budget -= work_done;
 		tot_work_done += work_done;
 		if (budget <= 0)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.h
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@ struct ath12k_vif;
 
 #ifdef CPTCFG_ATH12K_PPE_DS_SUPPORT
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_NAPI_WEIGHT 128
+#define ATH12K_PPE_DS_TX_CMPL_NAPI_SCALE 4
+#define ATH12K_PPE_DS_TX_CMPL_MAX_BUDGET 256
 
 bool ath12k_ppe_ds_enabled(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 int ath12k_ppe_ds_attach(struct ath12k_base *ab);
-- 
